   "id": "bava_metzia.103b.12",
   "daf": "103b",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "וּשְׁנֵיהֶם מְסַפְּקִין אֶת הַקָּנִים. לְמָה לִי? מָה טַעַם קָאָמַר: מָה טַעַם שְׁנֵיהֶם חוֹלְקִין בַּקָּנִים – מִשּׁוּם דִּשְׁנֵיהֶם מְסַפְּקִין אֶת הַקָּנִים.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «And the two of them,» i.e., the landowner and the one cultivating the field, both «supply the poles.» The Gemara asks: «Why do I» need the mishna to state this? The Gemara answers that the mishna «is saying what» the «reason» is for its ruling: «What is the reason» that «the two of them divide the poles?» It is «because the two of them supply the poles.»"
  }
